WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:07.966
Vulnerability, for instance,

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:10.301
is a real con in itself

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.012
because people use vulnerability

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.346
to manipulate others.

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:14.973
My brother's in trouble.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:16.266
He owes them money.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.017
How much do they want?

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.227
$350,000.

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:21.604
Well, the film sort of acknowledges

00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:22.856
this great truth

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.940
that all of us

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.359
in some aspect of our lives are not

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.236
quite what we seem.

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:29.529
We can't get through life

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.281
without being a little deceitful.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.991
You enjoy the show?

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:38.329
You’re a student.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.247
Mhm.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.331
Getting my PhD.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.750
First impressions

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.418
are only the tip of the iceberg.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:44.377
It's important

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.962
to really take the time

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:46.671
to get to know

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:48.965
somebody before you start

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.675
revealing things about yourself

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:53.553
or inviting them into your home.

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:55.055
Let’s face it,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.431
we’re practically strangers.

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:01.561
Money

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.396
can turn people into

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.648
their animalistic self

00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:08.193
because it is so necessary to survive.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.402
Don’t feel sorry for him.

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:11.237
You can’t cheat an honest man.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:11.905
That’s why we never

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.906
feel sorry for the mark.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.658
These are really smart people,

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:16.284
all of them.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.536
And they require you to be really smart

00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:20.038
to follow all their

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.456
strategies.

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:22.207
It's people

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:24.250
pretending to be people that they're not.

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:25.877
You really should not judge

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:26.878
a book by its cover.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:27.670
Behind it,

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:28.755
there's all these other layers

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.006
and things and intentions,

00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:31.049
and I think maybe it's

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:32.926
about asking ourselves

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.177
to be a little bit more vigilant

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:36.888
with what we are susceptible to.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.349
You ready for a test run?

